        <ArticleTitle>[Effect of subdiaphragmatic vagotomy on sodium and potassium distribution in the bodies of rats].</ArticleTitle>
        <Pagination>
          <MedlinePgn>528-30</MedlinePgn>
        </Pagination>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText>The state of sodium and potassium metabolism in the organism of male rats was studied by the organic distribution of these elements 1, 7, 14, and 19 days after bilateral subphrenic vagotomy. This operation proved to lead to disturbances of electrolyte metabolism, most pronounced 1 and 7 days after the operation. Relative normalization of sodium and potassium content was noted in 14 and 19 days.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
